5. Customer Service Changes

GlobalExceptionHandler now returns ErrorResponse instead of ApiResponse for failures.

CustomerNotFoundException -> HTTP 404 + CUS-001.

AddressNotFoundException -> HTTP 404 + CUS-005.

DuplicateCustomerException -> HTTP 409 + CUS-003.

MethodArgumentNotValidException and ConstraintViolationException -> HTTP 400 + VAL-001.

Malformed JSON and generic IllegalArgumentException -> HTTP 400 + VAL-002.

Unexpected exceptions -> HTTP 500 + SYS-001.

A private buildErrorResponse helper removes repeated response-construction logic.

6. Account Service Changes

AccountNotFoundException -> HTTP 404 + ACC-001.

CustomerServiceUnavailableException -> HTTP 503 + DEP-001.

Validation failures -> HTTP 400 + VAL-001.

Generic IllegalArgumentException -> HTTP 400 + VAL-002.

Unexpected exceptions -> HTTP 500 + SYS-001.

Existing dependency-outage behavior and HTTP statuses were preserved.

7. Important Design Decision

Error codes were kept in Java rather than an Oracle table because they are part of the application/API contract, not business data. Generic IllegalArgumentException was not falsely mapped to specific business codes. Dedicated business exceptions can be introduced later for cases such as inactive customer, duplicate address, duplicate account type, and invalid account lifecycle state.

